  "acceptance": {
    "id": "P06-ZERO-AUTH-T4-LOCAL-UX-CONSOLIDATED-CLOSURE-V1",
    "operator_result": "The unqualified TTY, narrow, plain and non-TTY screens explicitly continue locally without a login, setup/settings/configuration, API-key or documentation action; non-TTY never prompts. A real macOS PTY binary session selects the TTY transcript, waits for Enter and dispatches the TaskSeal-owned status continuation in-process. Unsupported selector, selector-local, argless-local and unknown-command routes stop at their minimal routing prefix without consuming or copying credential-shaped tails; plain and selector-prefixed generic routes now refuse at the boundary without reading any executable-position or later value. Saved-start access-token argv refuses from raw bytes before deserialization or argv hashing, and both inline access-token forms are explicitly proven to refuse before lock, serialization or any write while valid local commands and saved starts remain available. One offline successor gate binds OD-10/AUTH-01, current source and public inventories, every zero-auth call path, immutable Git history/write-set, all four parent-bound receipts and their topology, plus a sealed owner-worklog prefix whose valid append-only tail can receive the terminal review event without changing the PENDING checkpoint.",
